   "daf": "28a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "פָּסוּל וְאֵין בּוֹ כָּרֵת כּוּ׳. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי? אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: תְּרֵי קְרָאֵי כְּתִיבִי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that if one intends to consume the meat or sprinkle the blood outside its designated area, the offering is «disqualified, and there is no» liability for «karet for» one who partakes of it. If one intends to do so beyond its designated time, the offering is rendered piggul, and one is liable to receive karet for burning or partaking of it. The Gemara asks: «From where are these matters» derived? «Shmuel says: Two verses are written.»"
  }
